  "subtitle": "A toy video camera that stored eleven minutes of black-and-white video on a plain audio cassette",
  "why_scout_cares": "The interaction model is the medium: video is encoded as an FM signal and written to the LEFT audio channel of a standard compact cassette running at nine times speed, with sound on the right channel. A child's toy made the most mundane household object in the world — the audio tape — carry moving pictures. Later adopted by avant-garde filmmakers who built an entire festival around its shimmering, degraded image.",
  "search_terms": ["PXL2000", "Pixelvision", "Fisher-Price video camera", "KiddieCorder", "Sanwa Sanpix1000", "US 4875107"],
  "research": {
